{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"The `patch_command_body` command updates the source code of a specific Rust command within a control by replacing a designated code snippet with a new one. It validates the existence of the library, control, command, and implementation file, ensuring the old snippet matches the current code exactly before applying the modification and triggering a recompilation. This operation returns a status object indicating success or providing an error message if the target or snippet cannot be found. Patches apply to the stored code_body — the function body\nonly, never the generated signature. Preserves the impl record's existing readers/writers across the rewrite (a code edit never resets a gated command to admin-only). JOURNALED on the control's patch journal (facet \"command\", cmd = the name, op \"patch\", old/new = the two snippets, compile ok|err) - also when the compile fails, because the store has changed either way; revert = the inverse patch. The result carries patch_id when an entry was written, or journal_warning when the edit landed but could not be journaled. label is the stated reason for the edit, recorded on the entry (the why-harvest pairs it with the change; empty is allowed and records no reason); an empty author defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous.","import":"use flowlang::datastore::DataStore;\nuse flowlang::flowlang::data;\nuse ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse crate::dev::dev::compile::compile;","params":[{"name":"lib","type":"String"},{"name":"ctl","type":"String"},{"name":"cmd","type":"String"},{"name":"old_snippet","type":"String"},{"name":"new_snippet","type":"String"},{"desc":"The stated reason for this edit, recorded on the journal entry (the why-harvest pairs it with the change). May be empty, which records no reason.","name":"label","type":"String"},{"desc":"Who is making the edit, recorded on the journal entry. Empty defaults to the calling session's user, else anonymous.","name":"author","type":"String"},{"desc":"Request metadata filled in by the framework; pass an empty string from tools.","name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"slvzur19ed5ad5cc7k2c99","readers":[],"time":1794510445400,"username":"system","writers":[]}